# What the image build does not need, which on a working checkout is almost
# everything. `dev/Dockerfile` reads one file out of the context
# (`rust-toolchain.toml`), and `target/` alone reaches hundreds of thousands of
# files and several gigabytes.
#
# The name is `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore`, and Docker looks for it beside the
# Dockerfile it belongs to - here, `dev/Dockerfile`. It is deliberately not the
# plain `.dockerignore` at the repository root: that would be a new dotfile, and
# this machine's global Git excludes ignore every new dotfile, so it could only be
# committed with `git add -f` against the preference the excludes express. Both
# placements were measured on this host: `dev/Dockerfile.dockerignore` is read,
# and a root `Dockerfile.dockerignore` is not.
.git/
target/
models/
coverage/
backups/
.agent-tmp/
.ignored/
.logs/
.private/
private/
